.TH TANGSIBLE-TEMPLATE 1 "August 2026" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.SH NAME
tangsible-template \- debug a Jinja2 template against a real inventory host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tangsible template
.I path
.RI [ hostname ]
.RI [ "ansible\-playbook args" ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B template
renders
.I path
through Ansible's own templating engine \(em not a standalone Jinja2
implementation \(em by generating a throwaway playbook that templates it
via a real
.B ansible.builtin.template
task, delegated to localhost so the rendered file lands where Tangsible
can read it back, against exactly one inventory host. This is a
separate, standalone program from
.BR tangsible-run (1)
and friends: there is no tree here, just the render itself.
.PP
If
.I hostname
is omitted, the first host reported by
.B ansible\-inventory \-\-list
is used. Extra variables can be supplied with
.BR \-e ,
same as any
.B ansible\-playbook
invocation. If
.I path
lives in a role's conventional
.B templates/
directory, that role's own
.B defaults/main.yml
and
.B vars/main.yml
are made available automatically (the role itself is never invoked, only
its variable files \(em a template preview must never have side
effects). If rendering fails, the Jinja2 error is shown in place of the
output.
.SH VIEWS
Two tabs, Rendered and Source, switched with
.B Tab
/
.BR "Shift\-Tab" .
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B "Cursor keys, Page Up/Down, Home/End"
Scroll the active tab (also the usual
.B tview
vim aliases:
.BR g / G / j / k / h / l ,
.BR Ctrl\-F / Ctrl\-B ).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-A / Ctrl\-E
Same as Home / End.
.TP
.B e
Open
.I path
in
.B $VISUAL
(or
.B $EDITOR
, or
.B vi
if neither is set) as a foreground subprocess, suspending the TUI \(em
the same way
.B git commit
would. Re\-renders unconditionally once the editor exits, whether or
not anything was actually saved.
.TP
.B h
Open the "change host" dialog: type a new hostname, Enter to
re\-render against it, Esc to cancel.
.TP
.B /
Search the active tab's text; while a search has at least one match,
.B n / N
jump to the next / previous match.
.TP
.B q / Ctrl\-C
Quit. There is no interrupt\-vs\-quit distinction here (each render is
one synchronous, already\-finished
.B ansible\-playbook
invocation, never a long\-running process to interrupt). Ctrl\-C also
closes an open search prompt first, same as elsewhere, before quitting.
.PP
.B Esc
clears an active search if there is one; otherwise it's deliberately
inert outside the change\-host dialog \(em it used to quit too, which
made it too easy to close the whole program by reflex while just
browsing the tabs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, however the view was closed.
.TP
.B 1
.I path
couldn't be read, no host could be resolved from the inventory, or a
scratch file this view depends on internally couldn't be created.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: no
.I path
was given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tangsible (1),
.BR tangsible-host (1)
